  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 4 couples five actuators: each successful marker-bar grow raises the D marker by one 3-row band and simultaneously widens all four B-colored cantilever shelves by 3 cells toward the center. Tower buttons only reposition a shelf vertically; they do not widen it. A marker grow becomes a complete no-op if any newly widened shelf or the rising marker would collide with another shelf, a colored tower column, or the marker corridor. This makes shelf ordering crucial. I reached the eight-grow state with shelves stacked at y=6,9,12,15 and D at (31,19), and discovered that the two inner shelves must likely exchange vertical order while still narrow (around grow 4); after grow 8 their widths overlap and the order is irreversible.",
  "narrative": "Confirmed the resolver's 87-action prefix from a fresh reset and observed levels_completed=3 before exploring. Across four level-4 attempts, I decoded simultaneous shelf widening, collision-gated no-ops, the vertical cascade needed to clear successive marker bands, and the inner-shelf ordering trap. The best live level-4 state raised D from row 43 to row 19 (eight bands) but did not complete the level; no additional level was won. I stopped at 598 total env.step calls after spending the remaining safe budget on a fresh reproduction gate. That attempted 79-action shortened gate reached only level 2, so reproduction_verified is false even though the original 87-action sequence was observed live to reach level 3 at session start.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Only ACTION6 was available; coordinate clicks outside the five level-4 buttons did not reveal another verb.",
    "Level 4 button map: B tower (6,48)/(12,48), A tower (52,48)/(58,48), marker bar (28,54)/(34,54), left-inner C tower (6,57)/(12,57), right-inner 8 tower (52,57)/(58,57); left lowers/retracts and right raises/grows.",
    "The marker-bar grow is the operation that widens every shelf. Repeated tower-grow clicks alone change shelf height but leave shelf width unchanged.",
    "At the initial tower heights, five direct marker grows succeed; the sixth is blocked when the left-inner shelf at rows 24-26 meets the rising marker corridor.",
    "A collision-gated no-op still depletes the row-63 click-budget meter, approximately one cell per two clicks.",
    "A reliable route to eight marker grows is to keep shelves separated and cascade the outer and inner towers upward whenever the next marker band or widening edge is occupied; the observed eight-grow arrangement had shelves at rows 6, 9, 12, and 15 with D at row 19.",
    "The inner shelves become mutually impassable at large widths: one shelf's widening hits the other tower's colored column. A future attempt should swap their vertical order near marker grow 4, when the left-inner shelf spans about x=18..31 and the right-inner shelf about x=33..47, before they overlap.",
    "Retracting the marker with a shelf immediately above it drops the marker by one band; it does not create a hanging carry.",
    "Do not treat the attempted 79-click shortened prefix as valid: removing four apparently canceling probe pairs caused the fresh gate to reach only level 2. The supplied 87-action action_sequence is the live-confirmed starting prefix."
